From 459b7ca72c61e9799966306857973c19ef64221e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:10:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] misc: kona-caph: add MC74 ALSA driver (speaker + analog
 mic)

Plain (non-ASoC) ALSA card for the Capri CAPH/AudioH block; ASoC core
init hangs on this board. Playback runs DDR -> AADMAC -> CFIFO -> SSASW
(CAPH_IHF_THR_MET) -> IHF FIFO -> DAC -> handsfree speaker, capture runs
analog mic -> VRX PGA/ADC -> VIN FIFO R -> SSASW -> CFIFO -> AADMAC ->
DDR, in the order Broadcom's halaudio driver uses. 48 kHz S16_LE, two
periods (the AADMAC ring is two halves), polled from an hrtimer.

The AudioH/CAPH clocks are ungated here: mainline's hub CCU driver only
programs policy-mask bits for clocks it knows, so the stock masks
(MASK1 0x07ffb6a7, MASK2 0x1f800052, captured from the running stock
firmware) are ORed in and the policy engine restarted (GO|GO_ATL).
Touching AudioH/CAPH registers with the clocks gated stalls the bus.

Mixer: Speaker Playback Switch (DAC mute), Mic Capture Volume (VRX gain
0..63), Mic Capture Source (Mic1 = handsfree mic, default; Mic2).

Co-Authored-By: Vas <banoz@users.noreply.github.com>
---
